  "data_abstract": "The production of $\\rho^{0}$ mesons is measured with the ALICE detector in pp and Pb-Pb collisions at the centre-of-mass energy per nucleon pair, $\\sqrt{s_{\\rm NN}}$ = 2.76 TeV. The yields of $\\rho^{0}$ for rapidity $|y|<0.5$ are presented as a function of transverse momentum ($p_{\\rm T}$). The $p_{\\rm T}$-integrated and $p_{\\rm T}$-differential particle ratios $\\rho^{0}/\\pi$ are obtained in pp and Pb--Pb collisions. The nuclear modification factors $R_{\\rm AA}$ are computed using a proton-proton reference at $\\sqrt{s} = 2.76$ TeV.",
  "date": "11 May 2018",
  "doc_type": "publication",
  "doi": "10.1103/PhysRevC.99.064901",
